Before discussing specific kinematic cuts that define the \(\pi^{0}\) sample, it is worth mentioning that the \(A_{LL}^{\pi^{0}}\) analysis is separated into two \(\eta\) regions which approximately separate the large cells and the small cells. Figure 3.6 shows the distribution of 2-photon invariant mass plotted versus their pseudorapidity (of their parent \(\pi^{0}\), \(\eta\)-meson, _etc._). The outer black vertical lines represent overall \(\eta\) cuts of 2.65 and 3.9. The events selected here have all of the nominal \(\pi^{0}\) kinematic cuts (omitting the mass cut), which will be discussed later in this chapter.

