One might ask if the analyzed \(\pi^{0}\)s are primarily originating from the QCD hard scattering, or if a substantial fraction of them are coming from proton remnants or other multi-parton interactions. \(A_{LL}^{\pi^{0}}\) could be diluted by \(\pi^{0}\)s which do not come from the hard-scattering. Typically NLO calculations fold in these additional \(\pi^{0}\) sources, as does Pythia (provided we do not try to simulate gluons which are _too_ soft). One could instead look at forward dijet

